---
const steps = [
  { title: "Respond", copy: "Reply with the customer and enquiry context together." },
  { title: "Book", copy: "Connect the conversation to services and availability." },
  { title: "Remind", copy: "Keep the appointment clear before the customer arrives." },
  { title: "Review", copy: "Request a review and collect private feedback after the visit." },
  { title: "Return", copy: "See when a customer is due and continue the relationship." },
];
---
<section class="connected-journey" aria-labelledby="connected-title"><div class="container"><div class="connected-journey__heading"><p class="story-kicker">From first contact to the next visit</p><h2 id="connected-title">One customer record carries the work forward.</h2><p>Each step keeps the context created before it. Your team can see what happened, what is due, and where a person should take over.</p></div><ol>{steps.map((step, index) => <li><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span><div><strong>{step.title}</strong><p>{step.copy}</p></div>{index < steps.length - 1 && <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>}</li>)}</ol><a class="connected-journey__link" href="/product#product-journey">See how the lifecycle works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
